{"title":"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 38","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From a two-digit number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> we subtract the number with the digits reversed and find that the result is a positive perfect cube. Then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/d/1ade86291ac1199d4739e7e20504638724d99355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ {N}\\text{ cannot end in 5}\\qquad\\\\  \\textbf{(B)}\\ {N}\\text{ can end in any digit other than 5}\\qquad \\\\  \\textbf{(C)}\\ {N}\\text{ does not exist}\\qquad\\\\  \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{there are exactly 7 values for }{N}\\qquad\\\\  \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{there are exactly 10 values for }{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"297\" height=\"96\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c8b0d985d7137b67edcdd55029a03843223fe5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> representing the digits. The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> with its digits reversed is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/91637b4521e1c07f0aa214e1070b7c2f81c10967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10b+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />. Since the problem asks for a positive number as the difference of these two numbers, than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/082852571ecc48ed136ba13dcffa8f6e40064bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Writing this out, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46c3654faad3dc2bc47f215df3db00b01502294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10a+b-(10b+a)=9a-9b=9(a-b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"323\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, the difference must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the only perfect cube with less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits and is multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/7505050e0034432d1b03c656b92f39f0f04215e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^3=27$\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />. Also, that means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a67bd807313d0da2cc8762ec8e77d51216b5ef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b=3$\" width=\"72\" height=\"12\" />, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities of that, so our answer is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/d/3ad64e3ea9b87433e0db3974db4c05e1db652195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\text{There are exactly } 7 \\text{ values for } N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"288\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME\" title=\"1957 AHSME\">1957 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1957 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1957\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=19